anded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon elementor-accordion-icon-left\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon-closed\"><i class=\"fas fa-plus\"></i></span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon-opened\"><i class=\"fas fa-minus\"></i></span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">What is paternity, and why does it matter?</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t</h3>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-1491\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"1\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-1491\"><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; color: #000000;\">Paternity legally defines who your child’s father is. It matters because it unlocks rights, like custody, visitation, support, and responsibilities. Confirming paternity ensures both parents can make decisions about your child’s future and secure financial stability.</span></p></div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"elementor-tab-title-1492\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"2\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-1492\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon elementor-accordion-icon-left\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon-closed\"><i class=\"fas fa-plus\"></i></span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon-opened\"><i class=\"fas fa-minus\"></i></span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">How is paternity established in Lakewood?</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t</h3>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-1492\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"2\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-1492\"><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Paternity in Lakewood is established by signing a Voluntary Acknowledgment at birth or through DNA testing and a court order via Jefferson County Family Court. We walk you through each step, from lab work to paperwork, to ensure courts recognize your parental status.</span></p></div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"elementor-tab-title-1493\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"3\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-1493\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon elementor-accordion-icon-left\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon-closed\"><i class=\"fas fa-plus\"></i></span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon-opened\"><i class=\"fas fa-minus\"></i></span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">Can paternity be contested once signed?</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t</h3>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-1493\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"3\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-1493\"><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes, it can. If you signed a voluntary acknowledgment, Colorado law allows rescission within 60 days. After that, contesting requires solid DNA evidence and court filings. We support both mothers and fathers in seeking correction, clarity, or challenge when needed.</span></p></div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"elementor-tab-title-1494\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"4\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-1494\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon elementor-accordion-icon-left\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon-closed\"><i class=\"fas fa-plus\"></i></span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-accordion-icon-opened\"><i class=\"fas fa-minus\"></i></span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">Will I need support or custody orders afterward?</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t</h3>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-1494\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"4\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-1494\"><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Almost always. Once paternity is set, parents usually need child support and parenting time or custody orders. We help Lakewood families establish fair financial obligations and visitation schedules that reflect your child’s needs and your family’s unique situation.</span></p></div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is paternity, and why does it matter?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400; color: #000000;\\\">Paternity legally defines who your child\\u2019s father is. It matters because it unlocks rights, like custody, visitation, support, and responsibilities. Confirming paternity ensures both parents can make decisions about your child\\u2019s future and secure financial stability.<\\/span><\\/p>\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How is paternity established in Lakewood?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Paternity in Lakewood is established by signing a Voluntary Acknowledgment at birth or through DNA testing and a court order via Jefferson County Family Court. We walk you through each step, from lab work to paperwork, to ensure courts recognize your parental status.<\\/span><\\/p>\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can paternity be contested once signed?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Yes, it can. If you signed a voluntary acknowledgment, Colorado law allows rescission within 60 days. After that, contesting requires solid DNA evidence and court filings. We support both mothers and fathers in seeking correction, clarity, or challenge when needed.<\\/span><\\/p>\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Will I need support or custody orders afterward?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Almost always. Once paternity is set, parents usually need child support and parenting time or custody orders. We help Lakewood families establish fair financial obligations and visitation schedules that reflect your child\\u2019s needs and your family\\u2019s unique situation.<\\/span><\\/p>\"}}]}</script>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-29837cc elementor-widget-divider--view-line elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"29837cc\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b84f9a6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"b84f9a6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Talk to a Lakewood Paternity Lawyer Today</h2>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ffb90e1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"ffb90e1\" data-element_typ